Build is clean (0 errors, 0 warnings). Here's a summary of all breaking changes and fixes:

---

### Changes applied to this project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|----------------|-----|
| 1 | **TFM + packages** | `net8.0` → `net9.0`, EF Core `8.0.0` → `9.0.0` |
| 2 | **`HasData` with `DateTime.UtcNow`** — causes "pending model changes" exception at `Migrate()` | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, …)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — now throws | Removed the wrapping `ExecutionStrategy` + `BeginTransaction`; `Migrate()` manages its own |
| 4 | **EF Design package visibility** (SDK 9.0.200+) | Added `<IncludeAssets>` + `<Publish>true</Publish>` |

### Cosmos DB project fixes (for your separate project)

Your Cosmos DB project needs these additional changes:

**5. Discriminator property renamed to `$type`** — existing documents use `"Discriminator"`:
```csharp
// Add to OnModelCreating to preserve existing document compatibility
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

**6. `id` property format changed** — old docs have `EntityType|Key`, new format is just `Key`:
```csharp
// Preserve old compound id format for existing documents
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

**7. Sync I/O now throws** — replace all synchronous calls:
```csharp
// Before (throws in EF Core 9 Cosmos provider)
var items = db.Products.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// After
var items = await db.Products.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```
